JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARAKAWA KATSUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UMETSU KAZUSHIGE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOTSUYA SHINICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AMAKO, JUN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAKAWA, KATSUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UMETSU, KAZUSHIGE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOTSUYA, SHINICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A semiconductor chip having a high-aspect-ratio, high-reliability vertical-conduction structure; a semiconductor device containing the semiconductor chip; a circuit board and electronic equipment; and production methods for them.  A laser beam is applied to a silicon substrate (10) on a face orientation (100) plane to form an advanced hole (3), which hole (3) being then expanded by an anisotropic etching to form a thorough hole (4).  An insulating film is formed on the inner wall of the through hole (4) and a conductive material is provided on the inner side of the film to form a metal bump (30).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une puce de semi-conducteur ayant un rapport de forme élevée, une structure de conduction verticale à haute fiabilité, un dispositif à semi-conducteur contenant la puce de semi-conducteur, une carte de circuits imprimés et un matériel électronique ainsi que leurs procédés de production. Un faisceau laser est appliqué à un substrat (10) en silicium sur un plan d'orientation (100) de face afin de former un trou avancé (3), lequel trou (3) est ensuite élargi par gravure anisotrope pour former un trou traversant (4). Une couche mince isolante est formée sur la paroi intérieure du trou traversant (4) et un matériau conducteur est disposé sur la face intérieure de la couche mince afin de former une bosse (30) en métal.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>